### Examples for every endpoint. Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension, or copy the curls.
### Start the API first: `docker compose up -d` or `pnpm --filter api dev` (port 4000).

@api = http://localhost:4000

### Health
GET {{api}}/health

### Generate the 3 descriptions of a product -> 201 { product, descriptions[] }
### category must be one of the list in packages/shared/src/index.ts
# @name generate
POST {{api}}/api/generations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Stainless steel water bottle 750 ml",
  "category": "Sports"
}

### The same with a photo (multipart/form-data): JPEG, PNG or WebP, at most 5 MB.
### Replace the path with a real image. The response has product.imageUrl.
# @name generateWithPhoto
POST {{api}}/api/generations
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----describe

------describe
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Ceramic mug
------describe
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

Home & Kitchen
------describe
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="mug.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./mug.jpg
------describe--

### The photo as it was uploaded (only for its owner)
GET {{api}}{{generateWithPhoto.response.body.$.product.imageUrl}}

### Ids from the previous response (REST Client fills these in after you send "generate")
@productId = {{generate.response.body.$.product.id}}
@descriptionId = {{generate.response.body.$.descriptions[0].id}}

### List the demo user's products, newest first -> { products[], nextCursor }
GET {{api}}/api/products?limit=5

### Next page: paste the nextCursor of the previous response
GET {{api}}/api/products?limit=5&cursor=PASTE_NEXT_CURSOR_HERE

### One product with its 3 descriptions (404 if it is not the user's)
GET {{api}}/api/products/{{productId}}

### Save an edit; the generated text (content) is kept -> { description }
PATCH {{api}}/api/descriptions/{{descriptionId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "editedContent": "My own version of this description."
}

### What the AI calls cost this month (UTC): { month, calls, generations, costUsd, inputTokens, outputTokens }
GET {{api}}/api/usage

### Another month
GET {{api}}/api/usage?month=2026-09

### --- Errors (all have the shape { error: { code, message, details?, requestId } }) ---

### 400 validation_error: title too short and category outside the list
POST {{api}}/api/generations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "x", "category": "Cosmetics" }

### 400 validation_error: id is not a UUID
GET {{api}}/api/products/not-a-uuid

### 404 not_found
GET {{api}}/api/products/00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000ff

### 429 rate_limited (+ Retry-After): send the generation request more than 10 times in a minute

### Other statuses: 422 invalid_model_output, 503 llm_rate_limited (+ Retry-After),
### 504 llm_timeout, 500 internal_error (generic message; details only in the server log)

###
# The same with curl:
#   curl -X POST localhost:4000/api/generations -H 'content-type: application/json' \
#        -d '{"title":"Stainless steel water bottle 750 ml","category":"Sports"}'
#   curl "localhost:4000/api/products?limit=5"
#   curl -X POST localhost:4000/api/generations -F title='Ceramic mug' -F category='Home & Kitchen' -F image=@mug.jpg
#   curl localhost:4000/api/products/<id>
#   curl localhost:4000/api/products/<id>/image -o photo.jpg
#   curl -X PATCH localhost:4000/api/descriptions/<id> -H 'content-type: application/json' \
#        -d '{"editedContent":"My edit"}'
